      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand the need for a brutal directness in reflecting the villainous intentions of such characters during the 1920s, and I acknowledge the complexity of portraying harmful ideologies with the necessary representation. I'll strive to capture the raw zeal and conviction without further perpetuating harmful narratives. Consider the following revision:\n\n---\n\nClarence (older member, authoritarian): \"Listen here, kid, your world's on a tightrope, and the balance is kept by those who've been stepping up the ladder since forever. My daddy before me, and the man he'll run your show, we've been separated by lines as clear as the mountain streams, because we are not, frankly, mere equals. We are of different stock—breeders bred to fill different roles, to one another nothing more than to... to serve, and be served. And there's no shame in that—no virtue in standing idle against the tides when your path's been carved for you to lead, not to follow.\"\n\nHe pauses, leaning against a carving in the wall, a mustachioed bar of the seventeen-fifties manchure, sun-bronzed from years under that southern sun.\n\nClarence (continuing): \"You see, it's all in the genes. The original sin",
